// A std function that refuses its arguments raises a Colibri panic, which cannot unwind in the
// wasm build: the instance stops, but the page is told why (natively this is an ordinary panic,
// exit 101, which can be handled by nothing either).
// node-only: the wasm build ends the instance; natively the runner ends the program with 101.
// web-lost: yes
// web-stderr: panic: division by zero
import math

fn main() {
    print("before")
    print(math.floor_div(1, 0))
    print("never")
}

// expect: before
